            <ArticleTitle>Aortic stenosis and coronary artery disease caused by alkaptonuria, a rare genetic metabolic syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>302-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Alkaptonuria is a rare metabolic disease in which homogentisic acid deposits occur in various body tissues. We present a case of alkaptonuria which resulted in aortic stenosis and coronary artery disease due to homogentisic acid deposition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
